  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantChangesRelatedToRespondentCompanyAppearingInAnnualReportToStockholdersTextBlock id="HHFB056E8F64ABA7B86B31B31B7725CE20" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 16px;"&gt;12.) None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantChangesRelatedToRespondentCompanyAppearingInAnnualReportToStockholdersTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="HHC9E9219375AC2F82A8CDFAF00D88FECC" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 9pt; line-height: 14.4px;"&gt;13.) &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 9pt; line-height: 14.4px;"&gt;As noted in response to inquiry 3, o&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Proxima Nova'; font-size: 12.6px;"&gt;n January 1, 2026, NW Colstrip 370 acquired Puget&amp;#8217;s 370 megawatt combined share of Colstrip Units 3 and 4. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;"&gt;NW Colstrip 370 is a direct subsidiary of NorthWestern Energy Group, Inc. This is the first FERC Form 1/3-Q filed by NW Colstrip 370. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;"&gt;The Officers (including titles) of NW Colstrip 370 are as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;"&gt;&amp;#8211; Brian Bird, President;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;" /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;"&gt;&amp;#8211; Crystal Lail, Vice President;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;" /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;"&gt;&amp;#8211; Emily Ng, Treasurer;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;" /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;"&gt;&amp;#8211; Timothy Olson, Secretary; and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;" /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;"&gt;&amp;#8211; Emily Folsom, Assistant Secretary;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock id="HHD790CCB2EDB33AB49E3957CEAFD4E7D7" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 16px;"&gt;14.) N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;
&lt;table style="width: 511.5pt; margin-right: auto; margin-left: auto; border-collapse: collapse;" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 15pt; -aw-height-rule: exactly;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 506.2pt; padding-right: 2.65pt; padding-left: 2.65pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: #cdcdcd;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 2.65pt; margin-bottom: 1.5pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold; color: #b90101;"&gt;(1) Nature of Operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 18pt; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 18pt; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Times New Roman;"&gt;NorthWestern Colstrip 370Pu LLC (the Company), a direct wholly-owned subsidiary of NorthWestern Energy Group, Inc., owns a combined 370 megawatt interest in Colstrip Units 3 &amp;amp; 4, a jointly owned sub-bituminous coal fired generation facility located near Colstrip, Montana. This ownership in Colstrip Units 3 &amp;amp; 4 was acquired on January 1, 2026. We currently sell all energy and capacity associated with our ownership interests in Colstrip Units 3 &amp;amp; 4 to Mercuria Energy America, LLC under a Master Power Purchase and Sale Agreement. The delivery period of this agreement is through September 30, 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;
&lt;table style="width: 511.5pt; margin-right: auto; margin-left: auto; border-collapse: collapse;" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 15pt; -aw-height-rule: exactly;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 506.2pt; padding-right: 2.65pt; padding-left: 2.65pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: #cdcdcd;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 2.65pt; margin-bottom: 1.5pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold; color: #b90101;"&gt;(2) Liquidity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 18pt; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 18pt; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;During the three months &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; March 31, 2026, we&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; experienced negative net cash flows from operating activities, driven primarily by timing of fuel costs and low energy prices. As a result, cash generated from operations was not sufficient to fully fund the our operating and capital requirements for the period.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 18pt; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 18pt; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Should we continue to incur negative operating cash flows, we expect our parent company, NorthWestern Energy Group, Inc., to provide equity contributions as necessary to support our ongoing operations and to meet our obligations as they become due. NorthWestern Energy Group, Inc. has the intent and ability to provide such support for the foreseeable future.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 18pt; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: 18pt; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Based on the NorthWestern Energy Group, Inc.'s continued financial support, we believe that we will have sufficient liquidity to fund operations and capital expenditures for at least the next twelve months. Accordingly, the accompanying financial statements have been prepared on a going&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#8209;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;concern basis.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-size: 8pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HH26F298D96F05ADD051F0C74B218AC0A3" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4"></ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
